 ### [Screened Poisson Surface Reconstruction](6315-screened-poisson-surface-reconstruction.md)
-Screened Poisson Surface Reconstruction (SPSR) is an optimization-based method that fits a surface directly to a single oriented point cloud without prior training. It solves a Poisson equation to reconstruct a watertight manifold mesh, contrasting with marching cubes which may produce non-watertight results and require threshold tuning [6401-poisson-surface-reconstruction-for-mesh-export.md]. It is particularly suited for converting oriented point clouds, such as those derived from 3D Gaussian splats, into explicit triangle meshes for downstream tasks like physics simulation or rendering.
